- You wrote your last INR was 110. That can’t be a routine value — a true INR of 110 would be a life‑threatening emergency (very high bleeding risk). If you actually have an INR that high or are having any bleeding (blood in stool/urine, bruising, bleeding gums, severe headache, dizziness), call your PCP immediately or go to the ER.
