What to cover at your annual physical — suggested questions and checklist
1) Hypertension management
- Ask: “What should my blood-pressure target be given my age, AF, and other conditions?”
- Bring 1–2 weeks of home BP logs (sitting and standing if you have lightheadedness).
- Ask about medication interactions/side effects (amlodipine + lisinopril are common; check for ankle swelling, cough, dizziness).
- Labs to request: basic metabolic panel (BMP) or CMP (for kidney function and electrolytes), spot potassium, and urinalysis (for protein).
- Ask whether ambulatory BP monitoring or a med adjustment is warranted and whether one of your meds should be changed or doses altered.
