- For prednisone and sleep apnea: “Why am I on a prednisone taper for sleep apnea, and could this be affecting my BP or blood sugar?”

Labs and tests to ask the clinic to order before or at the visit
- BMP (creatinine, electrolytes), eGFR
- Urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio
- A1c (if diabetic or suspected)
- Lipid panel
- CBC (if concerned about anemia or bleeding)
- INR (if on warfarin) or confirm DOAC and renal dosing
- Consider ECG if not recent
- Urine pregnancy test if applicable

Follow-up/coordination
- If BP remains uncontrolled on 2 meds, ask about a hypertension referral (hypertension specialist or nephrology).
- If you need GI evaluation, ask Dr. Lee to include details about your anticoagulation and bleeding risk in the referral note so GI knows the anticoagulation plan.
